Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-28-2001||02:06 PM||||haven't found any yet.. but you see the tape on the lower manifold? heh.. there was tape on the side of the block too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> that SUCKED! heheh "..uum @$#@#$(&*(#$@#&&%& car won't start why the hell not..."  heheheh. Ramona left the tape on and just installed the gasket and manifold... she she had to re-disassemble it and yank the tape off! I tried to zoom in on the manifold with Photoshop but my scanner even at 9600dpi won't look decent into the ports. just pop the top off and look in it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  i can't wait to see wha tthe clutch and flywheel look like once you get it back appart. Your gunna use the current intake on the new motor right?||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||02-28-2001||05:25 PM||||Do you guys miss your Fieros at all? Must be strange to trade and still see your old car online.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||5
Z||000004||GT Bastard||02-28-2001||10:55 PM||||I kinda missed being able to just throw the GT in drive and go.  I went from a squishy ride that was super-easy drive to a stiff suspension and a race-clutch.  I missed the fastback styling and the super-clean interior of the GT, but the SE has won lots of respect around here racing.||||reg||1
